  "term": "bright light therapy",
  "definition": "Bright light therapy is a form of phototherapy that uses bright white full-spectrum light, often from a light box, to imitate natural outdoor light. It is used to help treat depressive symptoms in seasonal affective disorder and non-seasonal depression, and also some sleep and other mood disorders.",
